SDK thread priorities on macOS: map guest priorities instead of passing them to SCHED_FIFO
(perf pass 2026-10-11, stage 1c). Applied by tools/build_sdk_from_source.py
(SDK_BEHAVIOUR_PATCHES). FABLE2_THREAD_PRIORITY_MAP=0 restores the old calls.

PosixCondition<Thread>::set_priority and the initial-priority attribute passed the value straight
to SCHED_FIFO: the POSIX ThreadPriority scale (1/8/16/24/32) and the Win32-style 0/1 from XThread
creation flags. macOS accepts FIFO priorities 15..47 only, so 0/1/8 failed with EINVAL, and
"normal" (16) would have become a fixed-priority FIFO thread below every default (31) thread.
Now the value maps to a level -2..2 and a SCHED_OTHER priority 31 + 4 * level; normal leaves the
thread (and its QoS class) untouched. XThread's creation-flag priority now honours
ignore_thread_priorities (default true) like SetPriority does. Today those calls failed with
EINVAL, so the default behaviour is unchanged; with the cvar off the mapping applies.

--- a/src/core/threading_posix.cpp
+++ b/src/core/threading_posix.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 #include <rex/thread/timer_queue.h>
 
 #include <sched.h>
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 #if REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID
 #include <dlfcn.h>
@@ -71,6 +72,34 @@
                     "Legacy multi-object waits: re-check every 1 ms and spin while a handle is "
                     "locked, and let the audio worker sleep 500 ms when idle (A/B tests only)");
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+namespace {
+// FABLE2_THREAD_PRIORITY_MAP (default on, =0 restores the raw SCHED_FIFO calls).
+// Guest priorities reach here as the POSIX ThreadPriority scale (1/8/16/24/32 around
+// kNormal = 16) or, from XThread creation flags, as Win32-style 0/1. Passed straight to
+// SCHED_FIFO they are invalid on macOS (FIFO range 15..47, so 0/1/8 fail with EINVAL) or
+// would make a "normal" thread a fixed-priority FIFO thread at 16, below every default
+// (31) thread. Map them to a relative step instead and keep the default timeshare policy:
+// normal leaves the thread alone (and keeps its QoS), other levels move it 4 steps per
+// level around the default priority 31 (23..39, all within the SCHED_OTHER range).
+bool ThreadPriorityMapEnabled() {
+  static const bool on = [] {
+    const char* v = std::getenv("FABLE2_THREAD_PRIORITY_MAP");
+    return !(v && v[0] == '0');
+  }();
+  return on;
+}
+int MapGuestPriorityLevel(int priority) {
+  // Win32-style relative values (-2..2, creation-flag 0/1) stay as they are.
+  if (priority >= -2 && priority <= 2) return priority;
+  // POSIX ThreadPriority scale: 1, 8, 16, 24, 32 -> -2, -1, 0, 1, 2.
+  const int level = (priority - 16 + (priority >= 16 ? 4 : -4)) / 8;
+  return std::clamp(level, -2, 2);
+}
+int MappedSchedPriority(int level) { return 31 + 4 * level; }
+}  // namespace
+#endif
+
 namespace rex::thread {
 
 #if REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID
